      "section_path": [
        "Overtime & TOIL Policy",
        "Compensation basis"
      ],
      "text": "This policy governs payment and time off for approved additional work. Contract A and C have 40 contracted hours each week; B has 24. Eligible overtime is manager-approved actual work beyond the individual's contracted weekly hours, measured Monday through Sunday in the assigned workplace timezone. Absence hours, unused roster hours, and unworked planned overtime do not count as actual worked hours.",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": 2,
      "is_semantic": true,
      "list_level": null,
      "location": {
        "bbox": [
          63.599998474121094,
          241.38998413085938,
          157.51199340820312,
          259.2909851074219
        ],
        "element": null,
        "line": null,
        "page": 1,
        "part": null
      },
      "marker": null,
      "ordered": null,
      "rows": null,
      "section_path": [
        "Overtime & TOIL Policy",
        "Approval limits"
      ],
      "text": "Approval limits",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": null,
      "is_semantic": true,
      "list_level": null,
      "location": {
        "bbox": [
          63.599998474121094,
          264.5124816894531,
          530.4722900390625,
          351.4394836425781
        ],
        "element": null,
        "line": null,
        "page": 1,
        "part": null
      },
      "marker": null,
      "ordered": null,
      "rows": null,
      "section_path": [
        "Overtime & TOIL Policy",
        "Approval limits"
      ],
      "text": "Submit planned overtime at least one business day before work starts. Managers approve the purpose, maximum eligible duration, and Cash or TOIL compensation choice. Duration uses 15-minute increments. The weekly overtime ceiling is 8 hours and the total-work ceiling is 48 hours. Both controls apply; permission for 8 overtime hours never authorizes exceeding 48 total hours. Shift arrangements must also preserve 11 consecutive hours of rest. Emergencies require a documented HR exception review, not deletion of actual attendance.",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
